[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T6. Carbon Nanorings", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 150.9783477783203, 230.20321655273438, 172.68597412109375]}, {"text": "7%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.6215057373047, 304.6280822753906, 207.18873596191406]}, {"text": "6.1", "bbox": [172.68299865722656, 209.5625, 186.7479705810547, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.2", "bbox": [204.3090057373047, 209.5625, 218.37399291992188, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.3", "bbox": [235.93499755859375, 209.5625, 249.99998474121094, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.4", "bbox": [267.5610046386719, 209.5625, 281.6259765625, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.5", "bbox": [299.18701171875, 209.5625, 313.2519836425781, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.6", "bbox": [330.81298828125, 209.5625, 344.8779602050781, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.7", "bbox": [362.4389953613281, 209.5625, 376.50396728515625, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "∑", "bbox": [405.1860046386719, 209.5625, 411.47100830078125, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "10", "bbox": [174.0189971923828, 225.50250244140625, 185.41400146484375, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "11", "bbox": [205.64500427246094, 225.50250244140625, 217.04000854492188, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [240.11900329589844, 225.50250244140625, 245.81539916992188, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "12", "bbox": [268.8970031738281, 225.50250244140625, 280.2919921875, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "24", "bbox": [300.52301025390625, 225.50250244140625, 311.9179992675781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "20", "bbox": [332.14898681640625, 225.50250244140625, 343.5439758300781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [366.62298583984375, 225.50250244140625, 372.3193664550781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "83", "bbox": [402.6319885253906, 225.50250244140625, 414.0269775390625, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "In 2019, C18, the first example of a new class of carbon allotropes called cyclo[n]carbons (C𝑛) was de-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 249.4652099609375, 538.5745849609375, 280.5965576171875]}, {"text": "tected. Cyclocarbons are monocyclic, all-carbon compounds with high strain energy and low stability.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 271.28851318359375, 538.5846557617188, 284.8557434082031]}, {"text": "They can be generated and analysed by bond-resolved Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM). Cyclocarbons", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 283.2434997558594, 538.5640869140625, 296.81072998046875]}, {"text": "have interesting aromatic properties based on their π systems. C13 has triplet (3C13, spin S = 1), and", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 280.335205078125, 538.5785522460938, 312.73773193359375]}, {"text": "singlet (1C13, spin S = 0) forms.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 293.9571838378906, 200.2569122314453, 326.0678405761719]}, {"text": "6.1", "bbox": [78.60799407958984, 333.2664794921875, 92.84233093261719, 346.8337097167969]}, {"text": "Based on Hückel’s rule, fill in the table with the number of distinct aromatic (A)", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 333.2664794921875, 480.5848388671875, 346.833740234375]}, {"text": "and anti-aromatic (AA) 𝜋-systems present in each of C18, C16, 3C13, and 1C13.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 331.2522277832031, 480.5846252441406, 367.2721252441406]}, {"text": "Fill in all blanks.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 359.552490234375, 194.5926055908203, 373.1197204589844]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 371.50750732421875, 169.74588012695312, 385.0747375488281]}, {"text": "Number of Rings", "bbox": [121.06700134277344, 409.9095153808594, 204.8232879638672, 423.47674560546875]}, {"text": "C18", "bbox": [361.0950012207031, 385.0911560058594, 377.25439453125, 451.0435791015625]}, {"text": "C16", "bbox": [406.37799072265625, 385.0911560058594, 422.53741455078125, 451.0435791015625]}, {"text": "3C13", "bbox": [449.1700134277344, 385.09112548828125, 470.3104248046875, 451.0435485839844]}, {"text": "1C13", "bbox": [494.4519958496094, 385.09112548828125, 515.5933837890625, 451.0435485839844]}, {"text": "A", "bbox": [121.06700134277344, 425.8504943847656, 127.94061279296875, 439.417724609375]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [366.57501220703125, 425.8504943847656, 372.2713928222656, 439.417724609375]}, {"text": "0", "bbox": [411.8580017089844, 425.8504943847656, 417.55438232421875, 439.417724609375]}, {"text": "0", "bbox": [457.1409912109375, 425.8504943847656, 462.8373718261719, 439.417724609375]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [502.42401123046875, 425.8504943847656, 508.1203918457031, 439.417724609375]}, {"text": "AA", "bbox": [121.06700134277344, 441.7904968261719, 134.81480407714844, 455.35772705078125]}, {"text": "0", "bbox": [366.57501220703125, 441.7904968261719, 372.2713928222656, 455.35772705078125]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [411.8580017089844, 441.7904968261719, 417.55438232421875, 455.35772705078125]}, {"text": "0", "bbox": [457.1409912109375, 441.7904968261719, 462.8373718261719, 455.35772705078125]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [502.42401123046875, 441.7904968261719, 508.1203918457031, 455.35772705078125]}, {"text": "For C18 and C16: 2 pts each.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 469.59051513671875, 247.33372497558594, 483.1577453613281]}, {"text": "If both A and AA correct: 2 pts", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 481.5455017089844, 255.1537628173828, 495.11273193359375]}, {"text": "If one correct, one blank: 1 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 493.50048828125, 252.9503936767578, 507.0677185058594]}, {"text": "If one correct, one wrong: 0 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 505.45550537109375, 257.3439025878906, 519.022705078125]}, {"text": "Both wrong: 0 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 517.4104614257812, 193.82235717773438, 530.9776611328125]}, {"text": "For triplet C13 and singlet C13: 3 pts each", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 541.3214721679688, 309.4415283203125, 554.888671875]}, {"text": "If both A and AA correct: 3 pts", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 553.2764282226562, 255.1537628173828, 566.8436279296875]}, {"text": "If one correct, one blank: 2 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 565.2313842773438, 252.9503936767578, 578.798583984375]}, {"text": "If one correct, one wrong: 1 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 577.1864013671875, 257.3439025878906, 590.7536010742188]}, {"text": "Both wrong: 0 pt", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 589.1414184570312, 193.82235717773438, 602.7086181640625]}, {"text": "10.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 333.1914978027344, 526.921142578125, 346.75872802734375]}, {"text": "Later, cyclo[n]carbons C10, C12, C14, C20, and C26 were generated by a combination of dehalogenation", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 628.39453125, 538.5604248046875, 644.4527587890625]}, {"text": "and retro-Bergman (1) reactions on a surface. AFM images taken during the synthesis of C14 are shown", "bbox": [56.69300842285156, 640.3495483398438, 538.5792846679688, 656.4077758789062]}, {"text": "below:", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 652.3045654296875, 87.44817352294922, 665.8717651367188]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "6.2", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 362.5505065917969, 92.84233856201172, 376.11773681640625]}, {"text": "Draw structures B-D. Note they may contain one or more unpaired electrons.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 362.5505065917969, 480.59393310546875, 376.11773681640625]}, {"text": "The structure of A is given as an example.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 374.5065002441406, 309.9571533203125, 388.07373046875]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 386.46148681640625, 169.74588012695312, 400.0287170410156]}, {"text": "A", "bbox": [214.8470001220703, 413.03948974609375, 221.72061157226562, 426.6067199707031]}, {"text": "B", "bbox": [373.6449890136719, 414.1514892578125, 380.338623046875, 427.7187194824219]}, {"text": "C", "bbox": [215.10899353027344, 512.7145385742188, 221.4572296142578, 526.28173828125]}, {"text": "D", "bbox": [373.30499267578125, 515.9934692382812, 380.6796569824219, 529.5606689453125]}, {"text": "A is given to the students.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 633.697509765625, 235.84439086914062, 647.2647094726562]}, {"text": "B is worth 4 points. 1 pt awarded to incorrect structure with 3 Cl. 1 pt awarded to", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 645.6535034179688, 480.5719909667969, 659.220703125]}, {"text": "incorrect structures with 2 alkynes in 1,5-relationship, indicating understanding", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 657.6085205078125, 480.579833984375, 671.1757202148438]}, {"text": "of retro-Bergman. -1 pt if radicals missing or incorrect.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 669.5635375976562, 369.6246337890625, 683.1307373046875]}, {"text": "C is worth 3 points. Full points also given to alternating single and triple bonds.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 681.5185546875, 480.5727233886719, 695.0857543945312]}, {"text": "1 pt awarded to incorrect structure with 1 Cl. -1 pt if radicals missing or incor-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 693.4735717773438, 480.585205078125, 707.040771484375]}, {"text": "rect.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 705.4285888671875, 135.3839874267578, 718.9957885742188]}, {"text": "D is worth 4 points. 1 pt awarded to incorrect structure with 5 Cl. 1 pt awarded", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 717.3845825195312, 480.59173583984375, 730.9517822265625]}, {"text": "to incorrect structures with two alkynes in 1,5-relationship, indicating under-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 729.339599609375, 480.585205078125, 742.9067993164062]}, {"text": "standing of retro-Bergman. -1 pt if radicals missing or incorrect.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 741.2946166992188, 413.3106384277344, 754.86181640625]}, {"text": "11.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 362.4754943847656, 526.921142578125, 376.042724609375]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "6.3", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "The voltages applied during the AFM-mediated synthesis of C𝑛may vary. Us-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 156.3612060546875, 480.5843505859375, 187.4925537109375]}, {"text": "ing the given C–X bond energies, choose the possible halogen(s) in the halo-", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 178.18450927734375, 480.5812683105469, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "genated reagent for C18 synthesis via a retro-Bergman reaction with a voltage", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 190.1405029296875, 480.5830993652344, 206.19773864746094]}, {"text": "of 2.5 V acting on the electrons.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 202.0955047607422, 261.9289245605469, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "Bond", "bbox": [215.03399658203125, 231.67649841308594, 239.8232879638672, 245.2437286376953]}, {"text": "(C–X)", "bbox": [215.88499450683594, 243.63150024414062, 238.97634887695312, 257.19873046875]}, {"text": "Bond Dissociation Energy /", "bbox": [259.3330078125, 230.9355010986328, 384.88238525390625, 244.5027313232422]}, {"text": "kJ mol−1", "bbox": [302.03900146484375, 219.55413818359375, 341.6832275390625, 285.5065612792969]}, {"text": "C–F", "bbox": [219.2050018310547, 260.3125, 235.65367126464844, 273.8797302246094]}, {"text": "467", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 260.3125, 330.6595764160156, 273.8797302246094]}, {"text": "C–Cl", "bbox": [217.35899353027344, 276.25250244140625, 237.50148010253906, 289.8197326660156]}, {"text": "346", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 276.25250244140625, 330.6595764160156, 289.8197326660156]}, {"text": "C–Br", "bbox": [216.4949951171875, 292.1925048828125, 238.36373901367188, 305.7597351074219]}, {"text": "290", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 292.1925048828125, 330.6595764160156, 305.7597351074219]}, {"text": "C–I", "bbox": [220.1020050048828, 308.13348388671875, 234.75564575195312, 321.7007141113281]}, {"text": "228", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 308.13348388671875, 330.6595764160156, 321.7007141113281]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 335.5874938964844, 169.74588012695312, 349.15472412109375]}, {"text": "First, we need to convert eV to kJ mol−1:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 331.1982116699219, 301.849609375, 362.3295593261719]}, {"text": "𝐸𝑔𝑖𝑣𝑒𝑛[kJ mol−1] = 2.5 × (1.602 × 10−19 × 6.022 × 1023)/1000 kJ mol−1", "bbox": [144.21800231933594, 352.552001953125, 450.55975341796875, 392.715576171875]}, {"text": "(1)", "bbox": [468.9139709472656, 371.4525146484375, 480.58819580078125, 385.0197448730469]}, {"text": "𝐸𝑔𝑖𝑣𝑒𝑛= 2.5 ⋅96.485 kJ mol−1 = 241.2 kJ mol−1", "bbox": [191.87399291992188, 382.44000244140625, 402.90374755859375, 422.60357666015625]}, {"text": "(2)", "bbox": [468.9139709472656, 401.34051513671875, 480.58819580078125, 414.9077453613281]}, {"text": "The only candidate with 𝐵𝐷𝐸≤𝐸𝑔𝑖𝑣𝑒𝑛is the C–I bond.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 404.3580017089844, 366.9114685058594, 440.5365905761719]}, {"text": "X = I", "bbox": [124.05599975585938, 441.728515625, 144.13926696777344, 455.2957458496094]}, {"text": "1 point for unit transformation, 1 point for correct halogen choice.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 463.0484924316406, 423.9606018066406, 476.61572265625]}, {"text": "(2 pts awarded if I is chosen with no working)", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 475.00347900390625, 325.7666931152344, 488.5707092285156]}, {"text": "0 pts for other halogens or more than one halogen chosen.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 486.9584655761719, 391.7117004394531, 500.52569580078125]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}, {"text": "In 2025, the first relatively stable cyclo[48]carbon was synthesised. The molecule was stabilised by cate-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 516.6494750976562, 538.6016235351562, 530.2166748046875]}, {"text": "nation (forming interlocking rings) with macrocycle E and was first characterised by electrospray mass", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 528.6044921875, 538.5740966796875, 542.1716918945312]}, {"text": "spectrometry in positive mode.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 540.5595092773438, 201.94837951660156, 554.126708984375]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "6.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "In the mass spectrum obtained, four intense peaks were observed m/z: 591,", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 166.2294921875, 480.5869140625, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "783, 879, and 1174. Suggest the identity of these ions. Use integer atomic", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 178.18450927734375, 480.5853576660156, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "masses and assume no fragmentation happened. The ion corresponding to", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 192.4844970703125, 480.5472717285156, 206.05172729492188]}, {"text": "m/z = 591 is given as an example.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 204.4394989013672, 270.1251525878906, 218.00672912597656]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 216.39450073242188, 169.74588012695312, 229.96173095703125]}, {"text": "Molecular weight of E is 590 (C40H34N2O3). Molecular weight of C48 is 576. The", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 203.53213500976562, 480.5840148925781, 269.48455810546875]}, {"text": "first signal is given and corresponds to [E+H]+. The catenane with one molecule", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 223.960205078125, 480.57763671875, 259.9801025390625]}, {"text": "of E would yield signal m/z 1161 which does not match with given signals. Hence", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 252.260498046875, 480.5741882324219, 265.8277282714844]}, {"text": "we should consider the probability of di- and tri-catenation as well as dication", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 264.2154846191406, 480.5791015625, 277.78271484375]}, {"text": "and trication formation (question clearly states positive mode):", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 276.17047119140625, 407.8810119628906, 289.7377014160156]}, {"text": "m/z", "bbox": [160.9929962158203, 305.0115051269531, 177.68856811523438, 318.5787353515625]}, {"text": "+1H+", "bbox": [241.91299438476562, 280.1931457519531, 267.3329772949219, 346.14556884765625]}, {"text": "+2H+", "bbox": [327.44500732421875, 280.1931457519531, 352.8639831542969, 346.14556884765625]}, {"text": "+3H+", "bbox": [412.97601318359375, 280.1931457519531, 438.3949890136719, 346.14556884765625]}, {"text": "C48E", "bbox": [157.6199951171875, 296.1331481933594, 181.06253051757812, 362.0855712890625]}, {"text": "1167", "bbox": [243.47900390625, 320.9515075683594, 266.2712097167969, 334.51873779296875]}, {"text": "584", "bbox": [331.8590087890625, 320.9515075683594, 348.9526062011719, 334.51873779296875]}, {"text": "389.7", "bbox": [413.20599365234375, 320.9515075683594, 438.6681823730469, 334.51873779296875]}, {"text": "C48E2", "bbox": [155.12899780273438, 312.0731506347656, 183.05419921875, 378.02557373046875]}, {"text": "1757", "bbox": [243.47900390625, 336.8915100097656, 266.2712097167969, 350.458740234375]}, {"text": "879", "bbox": [331.8590087890625, 336.8915100097656, 348.9526062011719, 350.458740234375]}, {"text": "586.3", "bbox": [413.20599365234375, 336.8915100097656, 438.6681823730469, 350.458740234375]}, {"text": "C48E3", "bbox": [155.12899780273438, 328.0131530761719, 183.05419921875, 393.9665832519531]}, {"text": "2347", "bbox": [243.47900390625, 352.8315124511719, 266.2712097167969, 366.39874267578125]}, {"text": "1174", "bbox": [329.010986328125, 352.8315124511719, 351.8031921386719, 366.39874267578125]}, {"text": "783", "bbox": [417.3900146484375, 352.8315124511719, 434.4836120605469, 366.39874267578125]}, {"text": "Therefore, 783 and 1174 peaks correspond to tri-catenane [C48E3 + 3H]3+", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 358.2911376953125, 480.0861511230469, 424.2435607910156]}, {"text": "and", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 396.76849365234375, 132.56622314453125, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "[C48E3 + 2H]2+", "bbox": [140.7539825439453, 371.95013427734375, 219.72215270996094, 437.9025573730469]}, {"text": "ions.", "bbox": [228.40597534179688, 396.76849365234375, 250.6033172607422, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "Peak", "bbox": [270.8367004394531, 396.76849365234375, 293.3938293457031, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "at", "bbox": [301.581298828125, 396.76849365234375, 310.76519775390625, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "879", "bbox": [318.9560546875, 396.76849365234375, 336.0496520996094, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "corresponds", "bbox": [344.2311706542969, 396.76849365234375, 402.7914123535156, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "to", "bbox": [410.9607238769531, 396.76849365234375, 420.58441162109375, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "dicatenane", "bbox": [428.77386474609375, 396.76849365234375, 480.57904052734375, 410.3357238769531]}, {"text": "dication[C48E2 + 2H]2+.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 385.6101379394531, 224.6676025390625, 451.56256103515625]}, {"text": "m/z", "bbox": [143.83999633789062, 439.49151611328125, 160.5355682373047, 453.0587463378906]}, {"text": "591", "bbox": [210.87899780273438, 439.49151611328125, 227.9726104736328, 453.0587463378906]}, {"text": "783", "bbox": [281.77398681640625, 439.49151611328125, 298.8675842285156, 453.0587463378906]}, {"text": "879", "bbox": [356.3290100097656, 439.49151611328125, 373.422607421875, 453.0587463378906]}, {"text": "1174", "bbox": [428.0350036621094, 439.49151611328125, 450.82720947265625, 453.0587463378906]}, {"text": "[E + H]+", "bbox": [200.63400268554688, 436.5911560058594, 237.71498107910156, 502.5435791015625]}, {"text": "[C48E3+3H]3+", "bbox": [259.218017578125, 442.56915283203125, 324.0071716308594, 508.5215759277344]}, {"text": "[C48E2+2H]2+", "bbox": [333.77301025390625, 442.56915283203125, 397.5292053222656, 508.5215759277344]}, {"text": "[C48E3+2H]2+", "bbox": [408.3269958496094, 442.56915283203125, 472.0841979980469, 508.5215759277344]}, {"text": "4 points for each correct ionic species.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 495.2405090332031, 292.8528137207031, 508.8077392578125]}, {"text": "No partial credit as other answers will not have correct m/z ratios.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 507.19549560546875, 420.9838562011719, 520.7626953125]}, {"text": "12.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 166.15451049804688, 526.921142578125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 5, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-5", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Cycloparaphenylene (CPP) is another cyclic, highly-strained molecule commonly called a carbon", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5955200195312, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "nanohoop. The synthesis of the smallest known member, [5]CPP, is shown below, where PhI(OAc)2 acts", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 152.25897216796875, 538.5836181640625, 186.84912109375]}, {"text": "as a two electron oxidant.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 179.12950134277344, 176.75296020507812, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "(equiv. = Equivalent, excess = Excess)", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 617.5349731445312, 228.18240356445312, 652.1251220703125]}]}, {"page": 6, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-6", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "6.5", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of F-L.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 241.20362854003906, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 178.18450927734375, 169.74588012695312, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "F", "bbox": [191.07699584960938, 204.7635040283203, 196.5447540283203, 218.3307342529297]}, {"text": "G", "bbox": [294.031005859375, 205.6595001220703, 301.2451477050781, 219.2267303466797]}, {"text": "H", "bbox": [397.65301513671875, 205.70849609375, 405.2757568359375, 219.27572631835938]}, {"text": "I", "bbox": [191.87200927734375, 382.3924865722656, 195.74905395507812, 395.959716796875]}, {"text": "J", "bbox": [295.989013671875, 379.5694885253906, 299.28717041015625, 393.13671875]}, {"text": "K", "bbox": [398.1570129394531, 380.6155090332031, 404.7727966308594, 394.1827392578125]}, {"text": "L", "bbox": [190.99700927734375, 583.3355102539062, 196.6252899169922, 596.9027099609375]}, {"text": "24.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 166.15451049804688, 526.921142578125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 7, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-7", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "RUBRICS:", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 102.62214660644531, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "F: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 177.7135009765625, 99.56079864501953, 191.28073120117188]}, {"text": "G: 3 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 189.6685028076172, 101.30679321289062, 203.23573303222656]}, {"text": "H: 3 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 201.62350463867188, 101.7157974243164, 215.19073486328125]}, {"text": "I: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 213.57850646972656, 97.96979522705078, 227.14573669433594]}, {"text": "J: 3 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 225.53350830078125, 97.39079284667969, 239.10073852539062]}, {"text": "K: 3 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 237.48851013183594, 100.70879364013672, 251.0557403564453]}, {"text": "L: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 249.44451904296875, 99.72079467773438, 263.0117492675781]}, {"text": "Error carry forward can be awarded if the desired reactivity is shown and the chemistry is sensible.", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 261.3995056152344, 525.62353515625, 274.96673583984375]}, {"text": "-1 pt for each mistake in a part of the molecule not undergoing reaction.", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 273.3544921875, 403.9103698730469, 286.9217224121094]}, {"text": "For F and J, the di-anion of the product or salts (OLi/ONa) will be accepted for full credit.", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 285.30950927734375, 474.9710693359375, 298.8767395019531]}, {"text": "For H, the mono-anion of the product or salt (OLi) will be accepted for full credit.", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 297.2645263671875, 440.3526611328125, 310.8317565917969]}, {"text": "Next generation nanobelts were constructed from porphyrin rings and triple bonds using the template", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 326.95550537109375, 538.5537109375, 340.5227355957031]}, {"text": "synthesis method. Hint: M is the thermodynamic product and has four types of protons.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 338.9104919433594, 467.60308837890625, 352.47772216796875]}]}, {"page": 8, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-8", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "(equiv. = Equivalent)", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 585.7420043945312, 150.54385375976562, 620.3321533203125]}]}, {"page": 9, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-9", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "6.6", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of M-R.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 246.07862854003906, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 178.18450927734375, 169.74588012695312, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "M", "bbox": [231.8800048828125, 206.50050354003906, 241.27345275878906, 220.06773376464844]}, {"text": "N", "bbox": [354.64898681640625, 204.7635040283203, 362.74847412109375, 218.3307342529297]}, {"text": "O", "bbox": [232.61199951171875, 306.6654968261719, 240.5412139892578, 320.23272705078125]}, {"text": "Q", "bbox": [354.7349853515625, 308.8424987792969, 362.6642150878906, 322.40972900390625]}, {"text": "R", "bbox": [233.28799438476562, 488.0744934082031, 239.8648681640625, 501.6417236328125]}, {"text": "20.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 166.15451049804688, 526.921142578125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 10, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-10", "bbox": [377.97100830078125, 59.77293014526367, 538.6260986328125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8270263671875, 128.718505859375, 535.992919921875, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "RUBRICS:", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 102.62214660644531, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "M: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 177.7135009765625, 103.48579406738281, 191.28073120117188]}, {"text": "Substitution pattern should be determined with information on four types of proton.", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 189.6685028076172, 461.43438720703125, 203.23573303222656]}, {"text": "1 pt for any structure with one t-Bu group.", "bbox": [66.05799865722656, 201.62350463867188, 263.95257568359375, 215.19073486328125]}, {"text": "3 pt for structure with t-Bu added at both ortho positions, 1 pt for any other structure with two t-Bu", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 213.57850646972656, 529.2211303710938, 227.14573669433594]}, {"text": "groups.", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 225.53350830078125, 101.96385192871094, 239.10073852539062]}, {"text": "N: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 237.48851013183594, 102.19178009033203, 251.0557403564453]}, {"text": "4 pts if amine is given instead of the aldehyde (Delepine reaction). Does not affect the grading of the", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 249.44451904296875, 529.198974609375, 263.0117492675781]}, {"text": "rest of the parts.", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 261.3995056152344, 143.5178680419922, 274.96673583984375]}, {"text": "1 pt if Br instead of aldehyde.", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 273.3544921875, 203.03443908691406, 286.9217224121094]}, {"text": "O: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 285.30950927734375, 102.02178192138672, 298.8767395019531]}, {"text": "Q: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 297.2645263671875, 102.02178192138672, 310.8317565917969]}, {"text": "R: 4 pts", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 309.2195129394531, 100.6697769165039, 322.7867431640625]}, {"text": "- 1 pt if double bonds in porphyrin drawn incorrectly, this penalty will be applied at most once.", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 321.1755065917969, 505.22991943359375, 334.74273681640625]}, {"text": "- 2 pt if Zn is missing, this penalty will be applied at most once.", "bbox": [66.0579833984375, 333.1304931640625, 357.0661926269531, 346.6977233886719]}, {"text": "When aromatic rings are joined to form a macrocycle, oxidation or reduction can produce global aro-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 362.8215026855469, 538.5718383789062, 376.38873291015625]}, {"text": "maticity, in which π electrons are delocalised around the entire macrocycle. Only the π system forming", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 374.7764892578125, 538.5863647460938, 388.3437194824219]}, {"text": "the continuous conjugated pathway around the ring participates in this delocalisation. As an example,", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 386.7314758300781, 538.57470703125, 400.2987060546875]}, {"text": "[n]CPPs can become globally aromatic upon addition or removal of electrons. The number of π electrons", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 398.68646240234375, 538.5640258789062, 412.2536926269531]}, {"text": "is counted only along the bold pathway shown below.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 410.6414489746094, 307.1135559082031, 424.20867919921875]}, {"text": "When P6 is oxidised, it can exhibit global aromaticity and global anti-aromaticity.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 499.11248779296875, 432.7892150878906, 512.6796875]}]}, {"page": 11, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-11", "bbox": [377.97100830078125, 59.77293014526367, 538.6260986328125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8270263671875, 128.718505859375, 535.992919921875, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "6.7", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Based on Hückel’s rule, find the minimum number of electrons, n(e), from P6", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 166.2294921875, 480.58489990234375, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "that should be removed to achieve global aromaticity. Write the total number", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 178.18450927734375, 480.5758056640625, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "of π electrons, n(t), in the global aromatic system.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 190.1405029296875, 345.709228515625, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 202.0955047607422, 169.74588012695312, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "We should count electrons around the abbreviated structure of P6 as shown", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 214.05050659179688, 480.5887451171875, 227.61773681640625]}, {"text": "below:", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 226.00550842285156, 145.44618225097656, 239.57273864746094]}, {"text": "The total number of 𝜋-electrons is 14 × 6 = 84 in the ground state.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 407.531982421875, 418.59912109375, 442.12213134765625]}, {"text": "To achieve global aromaticity by Hückel's rule, we need 4𝑛+ 2 𝜋-electrons.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 419.4869689941406, 457.55450439453125, 454.0771179199219]}, {"text": "The minimum number of 𝜋-electrons that need to be lost is two electrons and", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 431.44195556640625, 480.5841064453125, 466.0321044921875]}, {"text": "the total number of 𝜋-electrons is 82.", "bbox": [114.6910171508789, 443.3969421386719, 287.746826171875, 477.9870910644531]}, {"text": "n(e)", "bbox": [182.48199462890625, 484.9005126953125, 199.1968231201172, 498.4677429199219]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [328.4070129394531, 484.9005126953125, 334.1033935546875, 498.4677429199219]}, {"text": "n(t)", "bbox": [183.156005859375, 500.84149169921875, 198.52381896972656, 514.40869140625]}, {"text": "82", "bbox": [325.55902099609375, 500.84149169921875, 336.9539794921875, 514.40869140625]}, {"text": "4 pts for fully correct.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 528.6945190429688, 214.22801208496094, 542.26171875]}, {"text": "2 pts if total number of electrons is wrong but it satisfies Hückel's 4𝑛+ 2 rule.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 525.7339477539062, 471.7403259277344, 560.3240966796875]}, {"text": "No partial points for the loss of two electrons.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 552.6044311523438, 328.2300109863281, 566.171630859375]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}]